<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mayenne</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mayenne is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, in the Pays de la <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/loire">Loire</a> region, named after the river Mayenne that crosses it from north to south. Its capital is Laval. The area corresponds broadly to the lands of the Gallic Diablintes and later formed part of the provinces of Maine and Anjou.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mayenne.jpg" alt="Mayenne" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Celeste (permission given to User:Oie blanche) · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pr%C3%A9fecture_Laval.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
